/// This message can be requested by sending the MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION
/// command. The position the system will return to and land on. The position is
/// set automatically by the system during the takeoff in case it was not
/// explicitly set by the operator before or after. The global and local
/// positions encode the position in the respective coordinate frames, while the
/// q parameter encodes the orientation of the surface. Under normal conditions
/// it describes the heading and terrain slope, which can be used by the
/// aircraft to adjust the approach. The approach 3D vector describes the point
/// to which the system should fly in normal flight mode and then perform a
/// landing sequence along the vector.
public struct HomePosition: MavlinkMessage, Equatable {
    public static let messageId: UInt32 = 242
